index 0000000..d868728
--- /dev/null
+++ b/SOLUTION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+# Solution
+
+Two bugs in `lrucache/cache.py`:
+
+1. **`get` did not count as a "use".** It read the value out of the `OrderedDict`
+   without calling `move_to_end`, so the recency order only ever reflected writes.
+   A key that was repeatedly read still looked least-recently-used and got evicted.
+   Fixed by moving the key to the end on a successful (non-expired) `get`.
+
+2. **`put` evicted on updates to existing keys.** The capacity check ran before
+   checking whether the key was already present, so overwriting an existing key
+   at full capacity dropped an unrelated entry (and left the cache under capacity).
+   Fixed by only evicting when the key is genuinely new.
+
+`python3 -m pytest -q` now passes (6 passed).
